{"page":"qftx-gauge-geometry","batch":"2","items":[{"id":"def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data","kind":"definition","domain":"mathematics","title":"Non-Abelian gauge data and bundle sectors","reference":"items/def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data.md","design_state":"Step 1 authored; readiness recording follows final scoped checks.","dependency_level":0,"deps":["def-countable-choice","def-lie-group","thm-the-tangent-space-at-the-identity-is-a-lie-algebra","def-principal-g-bundle-and-associated-fiber-bundle","def-smooth-principal-g-bundle","def-finite-dimensional-representation-of-a-group-over-a-field","def-associated-bundle-to-a-principal-bundle-and-representation","thm-associated-vector-bundle-is-well-defined"],"dependency_roles":{"def-countable-choice":"mathematical-premise","def-lie-group":"mathematical-premise","thm-the-tangent-space-at-the-identity-is-a-lie-algebra":"mathematical-premise","def-principal-g-bundle-and-associated-fiber-bundle":"mathematical-premise","def-smooth-principal-g-bundle":"mathematical-premise","def-finite-dimensional-representation-of-a-group-over-a-field":"mathematical-premise","def-associated-bundle-to-a-principal-bundle-and-representation":"mathematical-premise","thm-associated-vector-bundle-is-well-defined":"mathematical-premise"},"inventory_expansion_required":false,"statement":"Assume the axiom of countable choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Let $M$ be a finite-dimensional, Hausdorff, second-countable smooth manifold without boundary. A **non-Abelian gauge datum on $M$** consists of the following specified objects.\n\nFirst choose a finite-dimensional real Lie group $G$ that is compact in its manifold topology (every open cover has a finite subcover) and noncommutative (there are $g,h\\in G$ with $gh\\ne hg$). The actual group $G$, including its global form, is part of the datum. Its Lie algebra is $\\mathfrak g=\\operatorname{Lie}(G)=T_eG$ with the bracket transported from left-invariant smooth vector fields.\n\nChoose a smooth right principal $G$-bundle $\\pi:P\\to M$: the projection and right action are smooth, the action is free and transitive on each fibre, and there are local trivializations $\\pi^{-1}(U)\\cong U\\times G$ that are equivariant diffeomorphisms over each open $U\\subseteq M$.\n\nChoose a specified set $I$ of representation labels and, for each $a\\in I$, a finite-dimensional complex vector space $V_a$, a positive-definite Hermitian form $h_a$, and a smooth group homomorphism $\\rho_a:G\\to U(V_a,h_a)$. Here $U(V_a,h_a)$ is the group of complex-linear isometries of $h_a$, and a representation is the corresponding finite-dimensional group action. Its associated vector bundle is the quotient $E_a=P\\times_{\\rho_a}V_a$ with relation $[pg,v]=[p,\\rho_a(g)v]$.\n\nTwo smooth right principal $G$-bundles over $M$ are isomorphic over $M$ when a smooth diffeomorphism between their total spaces covers $\\operatorname{id}_M$ and commutes with the right $G$-actions. A **bundle sector** is one equivalence class under this relation. The datum specifies a set $\\Sigma$ of admitted bundle sectors and requires $[P]\\in\\Sigma$; a model may take $\\Sigma=\\{[P]\\}$. The Lie algebra alone does not replace the chosen group or sector. This definition does not choose a connection, an action functional, or a quantum theory.","provenance":{"statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable"},"sources":{"references":[{"title":"Matthijs Vákár, Principal Bundles and Gauge Theories (full text)","url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2110.06334","locator":"§§1.1.3, 1.1.5 and 2.1: right principal bundles, associated bundles, and the local-versus-global gauge distinction."},{"title":"Karl-Hermann Neeb, Differential Topology of Fiber Bundles (full lecture notes, 2024)","url":"https://www.math.fau.de/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/bundle-lect.pdf","locator":"Chapter 1, §1.4 and §1.6, printed pp. 8–15: smooth principal bundles and associated representation bundles."}]},"library":"mathematics","proof_strategy":"definition"},{"id":"def-qft