-valued forms use the graded bracket defined by alternating shuffle and the Lie bracket; in degree one, $[A\\wedge B](X,Y)=[A(X),B(Y)]-[A(Y),B(X)]$. Define\n\n$$\\Omega_\\omega:=d\\omega+\\frac12[\\omega\\wedge\\omega],\\qquad D_\\omega\\eta:=d\\eta+[\\omega\\wedge\\eta].$$\n\nThen $\\Omega_\\omega$ is horizontal and $\\operatorname{Ad}$-equivariant, and $\\Omega_\\omega=\\omega\\circ K_H$ for the imported vertical-valued curvature $K_H(X,Y)=-v([hX,hY])$. For any trivializing cover with smooth sections $s_i:U_i\\to P$, set $A_i=s_i^*\\omega$ and $F_i=s_i^*\\Omega_\\omega$. On an overlap, let $g_{ij}:U_i\\cap U_j\\to G$ be the smooth map determined by $s_j=s_i g_{ij}$, and write $\\theta_L(g_{ij})=g_{ij}^*\\theta_L$ for the left Maurer–Cartan form. Then\n\n$$A_j=\\operatorname{Ad}_{g_{ij}^{-1}}A_i+\\theta_L(g_{ij}),\\qquad F_i=dA_i+\\frac12[A_i\\wedge A_i],\\qquad F_j=\\operatorname{Ad}_{g_{ij}^{-1}}F_i,\\qquad D_{A_i}F_i=0,$$\n\nwhere $D_{A_i}\\eta:=d\\eta+[A_i\\wedge\\eta]$. The transition equations concern changes of local sections; they do not identify an arbitrary map $M\\to G$ with a global automorphism of a nontrivial bundle.","provenance":{"statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated"},"sources":{"references":[{"title":"Matthijs Vákár, Principal Bundles and Gauge Theories (full text)","url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2110.06334","locator":"§1.3.1, printed pp. 32–36: Cartan’s second structure equation, curvature horizontality/equivariance, Bianchi identity, and the local gauge convention."},{"title":"Karl-Hermann Neeb, Differential Topology of Fiber Bundles (full lecture notes, 2024)","url":"https://www.math.fau.de/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/bundle-lect.pdf","locator":"Chapter 5 §5.4, printed pp. 92–95, and Chapter 6 §6.1, printed pp. 100–101: connection forms, local transition law, curvature type, and local Cartan formula."}]},"library":"mathematics","proof_strategy":"direct"},{"id":"def-qftx-associated-covariant-derivative","kind":"definition","domain