imensional complex representation $\\rho:G\\to\\operatorname{GL}_{\\mathbb C}(V)$ that is smooth, and let $E=P\\times_\\rho V$ be its associated vector bundle with relation $[pg,v]=[p,\\rho(g)v]$. Define $\\rho_*:=d\\rho_e:\\mathfrak g\\to\\operatorname{End}_{\\mathbb C}(V)$, where the differential is taken after viewing $\\rho$ as a smooth matrix-valued map. For any open cover with smooth local sections $s_i:U_i\\to P$, write $A_i=s_i^*\\omega$. A smooth section $\\sigma$ of $E$ has unique local components $\\psi_i:U_i\\to V$ given by $\\sigma(x)=[s_i(x),\\psi_i(x)]$. Define the **associated covariant derivative** $\\nabla^\\omega\\sigma$ by its local components\n\n$$\n(\\nabla^\\omega\\sigma)_i=d\\psi_i+\\rho_*(A_i)\\psi_i,\n$$\n\nwhere $(\\rho_*(A_i)\\psi_i)(X)=\\rho_*(A_i(X))\\psi_i$ for $X\\in TU_i$. These expressions patch to a smooth $E$-valued 1-form on $M$, independently of the chosen local sections, and satisfy $\\nabla^\\omega(f\\sigma)=df\\otimes\\sigma+f\\nabla^\\omega\\sigma$ for every smooth scalar function $f$ on $M$.","provenance":{"statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated"},"sources":{"references":[{"title":"Matthijs Vákár, Principal Bundles and Gauge Theories (full text)","url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2110.06334","locator":"§§1.3.3 and 1.4.1, printed pp. 37–42: the induced associated connection, local covariant derivative, and Leibniz rule."},{"title":"Karl-Hermann Neeb, Differential Topology of Fiber Bundles (full lecture notes, 2024)","url":"https://www.math.fau.de/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/bundle-lect.pdf","locator":"Chapter 1 §1.6 and Chapter 5 §5.4, printed pp. 13–16 and 92–98: associated-section coordinates and principal-connection transition forms."}]},"library":"mathematics","proof_strategy":"direct"}],"requires":["lie-groups-invariant-fields-and-the-exponential-map","lie-algebra-representations-enveloping-algebras-and-pbw","fibrations-fiber-bundles-and-homotopy-exact-sequences","gauge-groups-and-representation-theory-interfa