## Completed item: `lem-aqft-invariant-quotient-exactness`

Claim: for a complex reductive affine algebraic group $G$, full AC, a finite-dimensional rational $G$-module $V$, and a $G$-stable subspace $N$, the quotient map induces a surjection $V^G\to(V/N)^G$ with kernel $V^G\cap N$, hence a canonical isomorphism $V^G/(V^G\cap N)\cong(V/N)^G$. Exact dependencies are `def-reductive-and-linearly-reductive-over-c`, `thm-complete-reducibility-and-reynolds-operator-for-complex-reductive-group`, and `def-axiom-of-choice`, all mathematical premises; `dependency_level: 0` because each is outside this run. The actual theorem statement and complete proof were inspected, including the finite-dimensional rational-module scope, Reynolds naturality, surjectivity of invariants, and explicit AC assumption. Current imported item, page, AC, and reductive-definition hashes match `research/math-imports.json` and the read-only source originals. The source treatment is Brion, Theorems 1.23–1.24, printed pp. 8–9, full PDF <https://ccirm.centre-mersenne.org/item/10.5802/ccirm.1.pdf>; fetched and read here. Owner context disposition and the imported item's judge-only historical stamp are recorded above without conflating them. No other invariant-ring supplier is used. No scoped validators have run yet; precheck remains pending. The missing batch-1 page edge remains open. Next: define the operator quotient using the finite local space, then prove the IBP/EOM/field-redefinition proposition using this exactness lemma.

## Completed item: `def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient`

Claim and conventions: for the finite raw polynomial space $W_D$ at fixed jet order, field degree, and engineering weight, the invariant scalar subspace is $V_D=W_D^G$. Given a specified $G$-stable raw identity subspace $\widetilde R_D$, its invariant relations are $R_D=\widetilde R_D\cap V_D$ and the exact declared basis quotient is $V_D/R_D$. The definition keeps the raw space distinct from its invariant subspace so the following exactness lemma can identify this with invariant classes in $W_D/\widetilde R_D$. Direct dependencies are `def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension` and `lem-aqft-finite-order-local-operator-space-finite-dimensional`, both `mathematical-premise`; `dependency_level: 2`. The quotient is exactly by the specified relation subspace and makes no exhaustive all-EFT redundancy claim. Burgess §2.1–2.2, Neubert §2, and Criado–Pérez-Victoria §§3/5.1 are context sources only; the local definition and subsequent proof determine the exact relation class. All four full-text sources remain fetch-verified; no scoped validators have run. The batch-1 A-page edge remains open. Next: author the action-level proposition and specify the boundary functional, leading variational derivative, and one-order formal field-redefinition convention.

## Completed item: `prop-aqft-integration-by-parts-eom-and-field-redefinition-redundancy`

Claim and conventions: for the finite rational $G$-module $W_D$ and its $G$-stable relation span, the invariant quotient is canonically the invariant part of the raw quotient, using the exactness lemma under full AC. A specified boundary functional annihilates compactly supported total divergences. A left Euler derivative for odd fields and ordinary Euler derivative for even fields is defined by the first-variation identity. For a $G$-equivariant, parity-compatible, compact-support-preserving local variation $F$ and finite formal action $S_\epsilon=S_0+\cdots+\epsilon^NS_N$, the explicit map $\phi\mapsto\phi-\epsilon^kF$ is constructed to be invertible modulo $\epsilon^{N+1}$ and changes the action by $-\epsilon^k\mathcal I(F^a\mathcal E_a^{(0)})+O(\epsilon^{k+1})$. It removes the matching EOM term at order $k$ while retaining the higher-order terms generated by the full pullback. This proves action-level fixed-order equivalence only.

Direct dependencies: `def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension`, `def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient`, `lem-aqft-invariant-quotient-exactness`, and `def-axiom-of-choice`, all `mathematical-premise`; `dependency_level: 3` because the operator quotient definition is the highest in-run supplier at level 2. Full AC is stated in the item, tied to the imported Reynolds exactness use, and carried as a direct dependency. Source context: Burgess §2.1, equations (21)–(26), and §2.2; Neubert §2, equations (27)–(29); Criado–Pérez-Victoria §§3 and 5.1. Their full-text locators, exact per-item extents, and limitations are in the batch-16 source-coverage JSON; all four fetch stamps remain current. No scoped validators have run. The exact batch-1 page edge is still open. Next: author `def-aqft-lsz-amplitude-data`, then prove the conditional fixed-order LSZ amplitude theorem.

