@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# Batch 25 authoring notes — Physical EFT Operator Contracts and Power Counting
+
+## Scope and plan comparison
+
+Owned pair: aqft-eft-operators / aqft-eft-operators-examples, order 981, physics library. The assigned design section and current plan-spec row agree on page IDs, title, companion, category/library, and all three A-page prerequisites: aqft-eft-foundations, qftx-gauge-geometry, and qftx-eft-operator-quotients. The plan-spec item arrays are empty planning placeholders. The registered physical contract is def-aqft-operator-basis-physical-data. The mathematics-page candidates def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension, def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient, the EOM proposition, and the LSZ equivalence theorem belong to batch 16; none is authored or reassigned here.
+
+The owner direction requires substantial B-page examples. The batch-16 mathematics example ex-aqft-operator-basis-reduction remains on qftx-eft-operator-quotients-examples and is not edited. Batch 25 adds separate physical examples on its own B page. The page edges remain exactly as planned; no shared plan was changed.
+
+## Dependency levels and current inputs
+
+Read research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-dependency-levels.json. Its stored input hash is stale: batch-dependency-levels.mjs check --run advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23 reports “Stale batch dependency levels … recompute before authoring.” A read-only computeRunBatchDependencyLevels call on the current manifests gives batch 25 level 3, requiring batches 2, 16, and 24; the current rows for 2, 16, 19, 24, and 25 are recorded below. The stored graph is run-wide scheduling evidence and was left for the owner to regenerate after the authored manifests drain.
+
+Direct item levels were recomputed from actual item dependencies before authoring: def-aqft-model-and-scale-data 1; def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension 0; lem-aqft-finite-order-local-operator-space-finite-dimensional 1; def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient 2; the four used gauge-geometry suppliers have levels 0, 0, 1, and 1. The assigned A definition is level 3; each B example depends on it and is level 4. This uses only the quotient definition, not the batch-16 level-3 EOM proposition or level-4 LSZ theorem.
+
+Current readiness was rechecked with loadStep1Record and step1Decision after the supplier owners updated their records. The four used batch-2 gauge-geometry items are ready. The batch-16 finite-jet Definition, finite-dimensionality lemma, and quotient Definition have current ready records. The batch-24 model-data Definition now also has a current ready record after its owner resolved the earlier Yang–Mills page hold. Draft status, pending precheck, and lack of independent approval are not treated as proof defects.
+
+The actual finite-regulator scale definition names the Wilsonian scale mu_W, heavy mass M, external-energy bound E, and regulator cutoff Lambda with separate meanings and imposes no numerical relation among them. The local-operator supplier uses a separate continuum finite-jet algebra and coefficient scale convention. The physical contract preserves the supplier's cutoff symbol Lambda and keeps Lambda_op distinct; identifying finite-graph data with continuum finite-jet data requires an additional map. No such map, generic functional measure, or continuum limit is claimed.
+
+The two page prerequisites previously tracked as open have current carriers and closed item inventories. The batch-19 qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-model page now contains its physical postulate and three other items, each with a current ready record; all five batch-24 foundation items are ready. The batch-1 aqft-susy-math-foundations page has twelve current ready item records, and the second required batch-16 prerequisite, reductive-affine-invariant-theory-and-geometric-quotients, is a published mathematical page. All three planned A-page prerequisite edges were rechecked against their current page and item interfaces; the cross-batch page rows are verified as scoped checks, not independent proof approval.
+
+## Completed A item: def-aqft-operator-basis-physical-data
+
+Claim and conventions: defines a four-dimensional, mostly-plus Minkowski, finite-jet physical operator contract containing field/statistics/reality data, gauge and flavor representations, the explicit compatibility condition between compact physical symmetries and the complex reductive algebraic action, a fixed canonical-dimension and loop truncation, the exact declared finite quotient, and distinct regulator, heavy, external-energy, Wilsonian, and operator-suppression scales. It makes no complete Warsaw-basis, generic error-bound, continuum, or empirical claim. Its Definition keeps finite-graph regulated data separate from continuum finite-jet data unless an explicit matching map is supplied.
+
+Direct dependencies: def-countable-choice; def-aqft-model-and-scale-data (formulation prerequisite); def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data (formulation prerequisite); def-qftx-principal-connection-form; lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi; def-qftx-associated-covariant-derivative; def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension; lem-aqft-finite-order-local-operator-space-finite-dimensional; and def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient. The maximum current in-run supplier level is 2, so dependency_level is 3. The gauge branch carries only AC_omega; no full Choice assumption is added.
+
+Sources read in full at the relevant ranges: Burgess, §2.1, printed pp. 13–15, equations (21)–(26), and §§3.1–3.3, on the one-order EOM field redefinition, power-counting class, and loop-order logic; Kaplan, §1.2 and §§2.4.1–2.4.2, on local operators, scaling dimensions, and gauge/global symmetry constraints; Criado–Pérez-Victoria, §3, printed pp. 9–10, equations (3.1)–(3.2), and §5.1, printed pp. 16–17, equations (5.1)–(5.3), on the first-order EOM limitation and higher-order terms generated by field redefinitions. Exact locators, dispositions, and verified full-text fetch stamps are in advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-25.coverage.json.
+
+Readiness decision is pending final authored-pair checks. The direct batch-16 and batch-24 readiness records are absent; do not mark this item ready unless those records become current after their owners complete authoring. Next: author both physical B examples, then finalize the batch manifest, contracts, coverage, source evidence, and scoped checks.
+
+## Completed B item: ex-aqft-scalar-gauge-operator-power-counting
+
+Claim and conventions: on a trivial SU(2) bundle, an even Lorentz-scalar doublet and its independent dual give the invariant polynomial $\widetilde H H$. At $r=0$, field degree at most 6, $D_{\max}=6$, and $L_{\max}=0$, its first three powers have engineering weights 2, 4, and 6; the dimension-six term divided by $\Lambda_{\mathrm{op}}^2$ has density weight 4. The antisymmetric bilinear is zero because the doublet components commute. The example specifies the real slice, the SU(2)/SL(2,C) representation pair, a zero declared relation subspace, and makes no completeness or error-bound claim.
+
+Dependencies: def-aqft-operator-basis-physical-data (same-batch formulation prerequisite); def-countable-choice; def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data; def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension; and def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient. The highest direct in-run supplier is the batch-25 A definition at level 3 (which itself uses the batch-16 quotient definition at level 2), so dependency_level is 4. The local proof verifies invariance under pointwise SU(2), the dual algebraic action, the zero polynomial identity, and the mass weights directly.
+
+Sources: Burgess, §§3.1–3.3, and Kaplan, §1.2 and §§2.4.1–2.4.2, support the selected operator-dimension and symmetry-counting conventions; the coverage file records each harvested section and verified full-text stamp. No experimental premise is used. The item has a complete four-step verification and a strict proof contract. Final scoped checks and Step 1 readiness recording remain pending.
+
+## Completed B item: ex-aqft-scalar-eom-operator-reduction
+
+Claim and conventions: for a compactly supported real scalar on mostly-plus Minkowski space with natural units, $m\ge0$, and the adopted free action $S_0=-\frac12\int((\partial\phi)^2+m^2\phi^2)$, the dimension-six density $\phi^2(\partial\phi)^2$ is related to $-\frac{m^2}{3}\phi^4$ by the explicitly declared total-divergence and leading-equation relations. The local map $\phi_{\rm old}=\phi+C\phi^3/(3\Lambda_{\rm op}^2)$ removes that derivative operator through order $\Lambda_{\rm op}^{-2}$ and induces the stated quartic coefficient shift. The argument derives the Euler derivative with the fixed signature, constructs the inverse through the retained order, and retains all induced terms at that order. It asserts no off-shell Green-function, quantum-measure, LSZ, or empirical equivalence.
+
+Dependencies: def-aqft-operator-basis-physical-data; def-countable-choice; def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data; def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension; and def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient. The local verification does not rely on the separate batch-16 general EOM proposition; it proves this scalar case directly. Its maximum current in-run supplier level is the A definition at 3, so dependency_level is 4.
+
