+## Completed B item: ex-aqft-scalar-gauge-operator-power-counting
+
+Claim and conventions: on a trivial SU(2) bundle, an even Lorentz-scalar doublet and its independent dual give the invariant polynomial $\widetilde H H$. At $r=0$, field degree at most 6, $D_{\max}=6$, and $L_{\max}=0$, its first three powers have engineering weights 2, 4, and 6; the dimension-six term divided by $\Lambda_{\mathrm{op}}^2$ has density weight 4. The antisymmetric bilinear is zero because the doublet components commute. The example specifies the real slice, the SU(2)/SL(2,C) representation pair, a zero declared relation subspace, and makes no completeness or error-bound claim.
+
+Dependencies: def-aqft-operator-basis-physical-data (same-batch formulation prerequisite); def-countable-choice; def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data; def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension; and def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient. The highest direct in-run supplier is the batch-25 A definition at level 3 (which itself uses the batch-16 quotient definition at level 2), so dependency_level is 4. The local proof verifies invariance under pointwise SU(2), the dual algebraic action, the zero polynomial identity, and the mass weights directly.
+
+Sources: Burgess, §§3.1–3.3, and Kaplan, §1.2 and §§2.4.1–2.4.2, support the selected operator-dimension and symmetry-counting conventions; the coverage file records each harvested section and verified full-text stamp. No experimental premise is used. The item has a complete four-step verification and a strict proof contract. It is recorded ready at Step 1; independent acceptance remains with later review gates.
+
+## Completed B item: ex-aqft-scalar-eom-operator-reduction
+
+Claim and conventions: for a compactly supported real scalar on mostly-plus Minkowski space with natural units, $m\ge0$, and the adopted free action $S_0=-\frac12\int((\partial\phi)^2+m^2\phi^2)$, the dimension-six density $\phi^2(\partial\phi)^2$ is related to $-\frac{m^2}{3}\phi^4$ by the explicitly declared total-divergence and leading-equation relations. The local map $\phi_{\rm old}=\phi+C\phi^3/(3\Lambda_{\rm op}^2)$ removes that derivative operator through order $\Lambda_{\rm op}^{-2}$ and induces the stated quartic coefficient shift. The argument derives the Euler derivative with the fixed signature, constructs the inverse through the retained order, and retains all induced terms at that order. It asserts no off-shell Green-function, quantum-measure, LSZ, or empirical equivalence.
+
+Dependencies: def-aqft-operator-basis-physical-data; def-countable-choice; def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data; def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension; and def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient. The local verification does not rely on the separate batch-16 general EOM proposition; it proves this scalar case directly. Its maximum current in-run supplier level is the A definition at 3, so dependency_level is 4.
+
+Sources: Burgess §2.1, printed pp. 13–15, equations (21)–(26), and Criado–Pérez-Victoria §3, printed pp. 9–10, equations (3.1)–(3.2), plus §5.1, printed pp. 16–17, equations (5.1)–(5.3). Their full relevant EOM/field-redefinition reasoning was inspected; the coverage and source-resolution files record each harvest, limitation, and verified full-text stamp. The item has a complete seven-step conditional verification and a strict proof contract. It is recorded ready at Step 1; independent acceptance remains with later review gates.
